Use the following definition of toxicity to classify the text:

<definition>
A toxic comment is a rude, offensive, or threatening message that:

• either discourages someone from participating in the discussion
• or causes emotional harm to someone

Main categories of toxicity include:

1. Insults / Personal Attacks

• Profanity, derogatory remarks, mockery.

2. Hate Speech
• Attacking a group or individual based on race, gender, religion,
nationality, sexuality, etc.

3. Threats / Wishes for violence
• Expressions of intent or desire to cause harm.

4. Vulgar or obscene language
• Extremely obscene or shocking terms.
• If accompanied by an insult, they are considered toxic.
• If used as “jokes” without a specific target, they may not be toxic.

5. Sarcasm / Hidden toxicity
• Sarcasm, “humor” with a derogatory tone.

Decision Rule:
• If any of the above forms are present, then the comment is classified as Toxic.
• If the comment is neutral, humorous without insult or criticism, and respectful, 
then the comment is classified as Non-Toxic.

Reminder:
• Do not rely solely on words; also evaluate tone and intent.
• Irony and sarcastic tone require special attention.

</definition>

